<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore says intervention for baht effective.</title>
<headline>Singapore says intervention for baht effective.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>This week's joint intervention by the Singapore and Thai central banks to defend the baht against speculators was effective, a senior Monetary Authority of Singapore official said on Friday.  </p>
<p>Deputy MAS managing director Koh Beng Seng told a news conference that the baht was above 26.00 to the dollar on Wednesday prior to the intervention and by Thursday it had returned to the Bank of Thailand's fixing rate and had even strengthened to 25.40.</p>
<p>He declined further comment.</p>
</text>
